{
  "_about": "How statement payees map to the labels used in the Freelance Payment sheet. Rules are checked top to bottom; the first match wins. 'match' is a list of lowercase words or regexes searched in the statement narration. 'label' is what goes in the Detail column. 'kind': expense (default), transfer (partner reimbursement or withdrawal: goes to the billing 'paid to' columns, not to expenses), ignore. Optional 'max_amount' / 'min_amount' narrow a rule by amount. 'fuel': true marks travel costs (petrol, CNG, Fastag) that are asked about when they fall on a non-shoot day of a personal account. Add a rule whenever a payee gets a new label.",

  "partners": {
    "_about": "Words that identify each partner's own accounts in a narration (name as the bank shows it, UPI IDs). Fill in once from a real statement.",
